# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository, on every platform.
#
# Every blob here is already LF; this keeps it that way. Without it, a checkout on
# Windows (or a Windows editor writing to a shared volume) rewrites files as CRLF,
# and since nothing normalizes on the way back in, `git status` reports hundreds of
# files as modified whose diffs are entirely invisible. That buries real changes and
# makes branch switching fight the working tree.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text files and leave binaries alone; `eol=lf` fixes the
# working-tree ending so a Windows checkout gets LF too, rather than only normalizing
# on commit.

* text=auto eol=lf
